WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.864
Industrial cyber risk does not fit neatly into traditional information-security assumptions.

00:00:04.864 --> 00:00:08.329
A loss of confidentiality may expose engineering information,

00:00:08.329 --> 00:00:14.392
but a loss of system integrity or availability can also affect machinery, product quality,

00:00:14.392 --> 00:00:16.990
safety, environmental conditions, and essential services.

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:20.455
Security decisions must be evaluated against physical operations.

00:00:20.455 --> 00:00:23.919
OT environments combine specialized control devices, conventional computers,

00:00:23.919 --> 00:00:28.683
industrial networks, safety functions, cloud services, remote vendors, and human operators.

00:00:28.683 --> 00:00:31.715
Equipment may remain in service for decades.

00:00:31.715 --> 00:00:36.479
Patching and architecture changes may require vendor support, testing, maintenance windows,

00:00:36.479 --> 00:00:38.211
and carefully planned recovery.

00:00:38.211 --> 00:00:43.408
Without a common framework, each organization or supplier may define security differently.

00:00:43.408 --> 00:00:49.471
An asset owner may request a secure system without describing risk or acceptance criteria.

00:00:49.471 --> 00:00:55.534
A supplier may describe a component as secure without explaining its capabilities or assumptions.

00:00:55.534 --> 00:01:02.030
An integrator may deliver a working process while leaving remote access and account ownership unresolved.

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:05.928
IEC 62443 creates a common language for these conversations.

00:01:05.928 --> 00:01:10.692
It connects business and operational risk to system requirements, supplier capabilities,

00:01:10.692 --> 00:01:12.857
service responsibilities, and lifecycle practices.

00:01:12.857 --> 00:01:16.755
It encourages teams to define boundaries, identify required communication,

00:01:16.755 --> 00:01:21.952
select protection based on context, and preserve evidence that decisions were implemented.

00:01:21.952 --> 00:01:25.417
The standards also reinforce that cybersecurity is continuous.

00:01:25.417 --> 00:01:30.181
Operations change, software ages, vendors release updates, and threat conditions evolve.

00:01:30.181 --> 00:01:34.511
Security must be considered during design, procurement, integration, commissioning, operation,

00:01:34.511 --> 00:01:35.811
maintenance, and retirement.

00:01:35.811 --> 00:01:40.575
IEC 62443 exists to make that shared work more consistent, accountable,

00:01:40.575 --> 00:01:42.740
and suited to industrial reality.
